WEBVTT

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:12.641
I'm not so fundamentally enthusiastic

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.382
Even I will participate in this

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:20.153
It's been a long time since we went for a drive

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.417
Everyone is excited

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.287
He's coming too

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.822
I may have no chance with him right now

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:32.563
But I'm definitely going

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:38.603
If you've got a good poker face

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.741
There will be something

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:45.812
Let's head to the mountains

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.781
We'll just get sunburned at the sea

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:53.920
Even though it's coat season

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.357
He is completely misunderstanding

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:02.595
What's going on?

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:06.566
Being this happy

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:14.439
I'm laughing so hard I might burst

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:22.982
I get choked up when I see his back

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:30.889
In the whirlpool of an endless smile

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.363
Here is the contact information and a pamphlet

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.456
for the funeral directors that
handled Lise's funeral.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.558
Thank you very much.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.837
Do you have some sort of business with them?

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:46.005
No, my father just wanted some
information on them.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:49.338
I see, well they were very
competent and respectful.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.242
Were they?

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.968
I'll tell my father that.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:56.850
For me, getting back to work has helped
me get my mind off Lise's death,

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.648
but my wife is still going through a lot of pain.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.412
I see...

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:04.782
I suppose it will take her a
while yet to get over this.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.392
Do you think so?

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.953
We still haven't been able to find that diary
that the two of you kept together.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:16.669
Maybe she lost it.
I'm sorry if that's what happened.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.193
Not at all...

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:22.208
I'd really like to have you drop
by if you're ever in the area.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.343
Okay.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.038
You're welcome at any time.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:28.537
Please give my best to your wife.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.082
Sure.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:42.252
Episode #9
Awakening

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.331
Well, how are you feeling?

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.839
I just kinda ran out of breath.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:53.573
Really?

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.107
But I'm okay now. If I just take it
easy like this, I feel better.
Really?

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:58.441
But I'm okay now. If I just take it
easy like this, I feel better.

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:04.717
Anna and I, we're talking about going to the
amusement park once I get better.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:05.718
The amusement park?

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.221
What Mireille said she wants to do
more than the rides and stuff

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:11.224
when she gets there is get one those hotdogs!

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.055
Oh? Really?

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.454
Herve, don't you remember those?

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.664
The three of us went and had
them together, you know.

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:23.770
You took us to that little shop.
God, the toppings were so spicy!

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.939
Oh yeah, that chili pepper sauce!

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:29.875
Yeah, that! We'd never had anything
like that here before!

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.045
Yeah, no one here could make
anything like that.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.881
Really? Oh, but those are to die for.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.417
Don't you think they're a little too spicy?

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:38.351
You think?

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.686
Well I guess we have no choice.

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.278
We have to go to that shop!

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:44.148
Yeah, I guess so.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:53.666
Ivan?

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:54.200
Yes?

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:54.701
Compile all that data.
Yes?

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:55.668
Compile all that data.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.760
Understood.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.426
The results are all as expected.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.140
Herve, what brings you here?

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:08.544
When are you going to have Mireille
switch over to the new medication?

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:12.185
Ah, that. This morning we received
a report from the lab...

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:14.346
Dr. Bender, we've got it ready for you.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.222
Here's that data.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.189
Oh?

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.215
I see, I'll be right there.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:20.727
I'll stop by the room later...

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:21.261
And when will that be?
I'll stop by the room later...

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:21.828
And when will that be?

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.062
I think I'll have some time this evening.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:23.863
Do you mean it?

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:24.163
Yes, I'm pretty sure.
Do you mean it?

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:24.697
Yes, I'm pretty sure.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:25.098
Yes, I'm pretty sure.
Dr. Bender?

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:25.928
Dr. Bender?

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.167
Dr. Nelson for you on line two.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.037
Okay, tell him to come here right
away and be on standby.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:32.205
Doctor!
Understood.

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:34.503
And you'll hand over the medication
at that time, right?

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:37.443
I'm sorry, right now, we're in
the final stages here.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:41.937
Doctor, just the medication...
Just Mireille's medication...

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:45.583
I know, Herve. You don't need to worry.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.287
Really?

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:49.312
Really, I'll see you later.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.721
All right, let's get started. Next...

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.036
You plan on looking for another job?

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:09.202
Do I have a choice? I gotta eat and
I gotta pay rent by tomorrow.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:13.371
Tomorrow!? How are you going
to pay that on time?

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:17.580
If I tell her I've found a job,
she might give me a little more time.

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.377
Claire, since you're so broke...

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:23.523
Why not go borrow some cash
from your brother?

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.557
What?!

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.492
He's living in uptown, right?

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.994
It seems like he's raking in the cash.

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:32.298
Listen, his money is my dad's money,

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:35.426
and you know how much I detest that man.

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:37.426
I know...

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.670
But it wouldn't be like you'd have to bow
down before your dad to get it.

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:42.742
They say beggars can't be choosers...

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:44.505
Oh, shut the hell up!

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:45.878
Just shut up!

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:48.870
That's why I am trying to hang on
without their help!

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:52.452
Even if he's my damn brother,
I don't wanna owe him anything!

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:53.853
Wh... Where are you going?

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.922
I'm going to find a damn job, what else?!

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.446
I'll have one by the end of the day!

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:00.148
But what if you can't find anything?

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:04.786
I'm sorry!

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.301
I, uh... My phone line was disconnected.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:45.532
And I suppose your service was cut off
just like that for no reason?

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.607
I see, so there was a reason.

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:52.245
Well, I'm sorry but it looks like we
already hired someone else.

00:06:52.245 --> 00:06:55.078
You won't get any base pay,
but you can work for tips.

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:58.580
But there ain't a lot of customers who
tip high-schoolers, ya know.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:02.181
Up until just a while ago we had
a bed-making position open,

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:04.747
but we don't really have any jobs
available for someone like you.

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:11.931
God dammit... What are you going to do?

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:12.999
Welcome home.

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:13.966
What?

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.171
Your rent's not due 'til tomorrow,
but how you coming with the money?

00:07:18.171 --> 00:07:20.773
Um... Can you wait for it just a little longer?

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:21.407
No, I can't wait any more.
Um... Can you wait for it just a little longer?

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:22.601
No, I can't wait any more.

00:07:23.176 --> 00:07:27.169
If you can't get the money, start packing
your bags tonight, honey.

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:51.331
This ham is divine.

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:53.372
Want to try a bite?

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:54.740
No, that's all right.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.611
J.C., you should try to eat a little more.

00:07:58.611 --> 00:07:59.612
Why do you say that?

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:01.247
You just look so frail.

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:01.981
Really?

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:02.515
And you're very pale.
Really?

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:03.316
And you're very pale.

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:05.051
What does being pale have to do with anything?

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:06.986
Besides, I usually eat a big breakfast.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:07.820
Just eating that?

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.311
Cereal is nutritionally balanced.

00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:14.619
Huh?

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.328
Your following us around cramps my style.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:22.134
What do you want?

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:23.536
I, uh...

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:25.838
We work during the day.

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:28.204
You could follow us around all day,
but you won't find out anything.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:31.010
Lula, it's time we get back to work.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.409
Ah, so it is.

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:33.980
Where...

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:35.147
What?

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.638
Where is that?

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:44.221
Where our bodies are being kept, that place?

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:49.161
Why don't you head back? I'll be there shortly.

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:50.150
Sure.

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:55.961
The more you know, the more danger you are in.

00:08:56.636 --> 00:09:00.402
Are you strong enough to protect yourself?

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:23.129
Are you coming in?

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:24.357
Uh, no.

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:29.500
We've been caught in the enemy's trap.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:32.564
The enemy's trap?

00:09:33.005 --> 00:09:36.463
Yes, this is what the enemy
has been after along!

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:44.010
Your "New Body"! Lise was attacked
because the enemy wanted hers.

00:09:44.984 --> 00:09:46.349
Lise?

00:09:46.886 --> 00:09:50.617
We saved Lise along with all of you.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:56.154
However, Lise was attacked when
we were taking her back home.

00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:59.865
So, Lise was taken?

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:05.167
Yes, that New Body fell into
the hands of the enemy,

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:09.867
and we put her real body in the woods.

00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:13.777
The woods? You mean the woods
where they found her body?

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:19.574
Yes, as her New Body had been taken,
we had no other choice.

00:10:22.188 --> 00:10:25.057
This enemy, which we've been
fighting for a long time,

00:10:25.057 --> 00:10:27.150
is a clan called Dolore.

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:29.224
Dolore?

00:10:29.662 --> 00:10:31.755
Their clan is on the verge of dying out.

00:10:32.832 --> 00:10:35.167
They continue their fall into ruin,

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:36.502
and if they don't find a way to lift the curse,

00:10:36.502 --> 00:10:37.970
there will be nothing they can do to stop it.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.572
Why?

00:10:39.572 --> 00:10:43.975
Because soon, there won't be any
women left to produce offspring.

00:10:45.077 --> 00:10:47.313
The condition manifests in the women
when they are young.

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:50.449
Like those you fight against,
they morph into monster-like creatures

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:52.383
and their former selves cease to exist.

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:54.353
Because of a curse.

00:10:54.353 --> 00:10:55.354
A curse?

00:10:55.354 --> 00:10:56.912
Yeah, a curse.

00:10:57.857 --> 00:11:00.758
Even if I were to tell you about it now,
I don't think you'd understand.

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:07.656
At any rate, they're desperately trying to make
women that can adapt to their bloodline.

00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:09.268
Make?

00:11:09.268 --> 00:11:10.826
In the literal sense of the word.

00:11:11.137 --> 00:11:13.606
They carry out test after test on human bodies.

00:11:13.606 --> 00:11:16.234
And after their many failures,

00:11:16.542 --> 00:11:18.442
they've now got their sights
set on this New Body.

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:22.413
In other words, this isn't just
someone else's problem.

00:11:22.648 --> 00:11:24.343
This is you girls' problem.

00:11:25.584 --> 00:11:29.748
There's no saying when they'll attack
and try to take your bodies.

00:11:30.423 --> 00:11:33.492
They're going to try to take us?

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:35.892
Yes, and that's why I asked you...

00:11:36.328 --> 00:11:38.228
Do you think you can protect yourself?

00:11:38.764 --> 00:11:40.254
Are you that strong?

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.633
The more you know, the further
you'll be drawn in.

00:11:48.474 --> 00:11:52.274
We have been waiting for this
moment for a long, long time.

00:11:52.878 --> 00:11:53.979
We have.

00:11:53.979 --> 00:11:56.348
If we succeed, we'll have made it possible

00:11:56.348 --> 00:12:00.216
to welcome a new member
into our family, correct?

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.082
That's right.

00:12:03.055 --> 00:12:04.249
Do it.

00:12:32.518 --> 00:12:33.586
We did it!

00:12:33.586 --> 00:12:34.720
It's a success!

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:36.415
It was all worth it!

00:12:38.324 --> 00:12:39.725
You did it!

00:12:39.725 --> 00:12:41.022
Thank you.

00:13:16.962 --> 00:13:18.430
That's not fair!

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:19.556
Huh? Why?

00:13:40.486 --> 00:13:41.680
Well...

00:13:42.288 --> 00:13:45.018
You're Claire, right? Hello!

00:13:50.062 --> 00:13:52.292
What the hell is this?

00:13:52.731 --> 00:13:56.827
I'm so sorry to keep you waiting.
The President will be right with you.

00:13:56.969 --> 00:13:58.037
President?

00:13:58.037 --> 00:14:00.870
Oh, I suppose in your case I should
be saying your brother.

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:02.675
Would you care for another cup of coffee?

00:14:02.675 --> 00:14:03.972
Ah, no...

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:11.074
Yo, Claire! Long time, no see!

00:14:11.217 --> 00:14:13.082
Yeah...

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:15.921
And this is the second story.

00:14:15.921 --> 00:14:17.548
We took out the next floor
to open up the ceiling.

00:14:18.023 --> 00:14:20.192
I'm gradually turning it into a museum

00:14:20.192 --> 00:14:21.887
and thinking about opening it
up to the general public.

00:14:22.761 --> 00:14:26.398
I've collected pieces from young
artists all over the world.

00:14:26.398 --> 00:14:27.433
Hi, Randy!

00:14:27.433 --> 00:14:28.734
Hi, Fred!

00:14:28.734 --> 00:14:30.861
What do you think? It's pretty cool isn't it?

00:14:31.203 --> 00:14:32.705
Um, yeah...

00:14:32.705 --> 00:14:35.697
I'm buying up all the works of the
promising young artists that I find.

00:14:36.175 --> 00:14:39.008
And then I'm going to set up an on-line art mall.

00:14:39.211 --> 00:14:41.145
And if you do that, then what?

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:43.182
With our own hands, we'll create a market

00:14:43.182 --> 00:14:46.151
where people the world over
can buy objects d'art.

00:14:46.418 --> 00:14:48.821
And you borrowed the money from Dad?

00:14:48.821 --> 00:14:51.346
Yeah, I borrowed the start-up capital from Dad.

00:14:51.557 --> 00:14:52.858
How much?

00:14:52.858 --> 00:14:54.393
Hey, don't worry yourself about it.

00:14:54.393 --> 00:14:57.624
I'm starting to bring in lots of money
from other investors too.

00:14:58.097 --> 00:15:00.399
As long as one has money,
they can do anything.

00:15:00.399 --> 00:15:01.832
Are you sure about that?

00:15:02.301 --> 00:15:03.602
What are you talking about!?

00:15:03.602 --> 00:15:06.196
I don't think Dad's that optimistic
when it comes to money.

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:08.540
Besides, I wouldn't trust a guy like him anyway.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.109
Hey, it'll be just fine!

00:15:10.109 --> 00:15:12.873
I want to prove that I can get
by without his help.

00:15:13.512 --> 00:15:16.715
I'm going to pay him back after
I make my first sale.

00:15:16.715 --> 00:15:18.649
There's no way this business is going to fail!

00:15:19.251 --> 00:15:21.446
As soon as next month rolls around,
you'll see too.

00:15:22.421 --> 00:15:23.388
Well?

00:15:23.789 --> 00:15:24.423
Huh?

00:15:24.423 --> 00:15:24.924
Why did you come here today?
Huh?

00:15:24.924 --> 00:15:25.583
Why did you come here today?

00:15:26.258 --> 00:15:27.059
Um...

00:15:27.059 --> 00:15:27.660
You came to ask me a favor, didn't you?
Um...

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:29.228
You came to ask me a favor, didn't you?

00:15:29.228 --> 00:15:32.220
Um, well...

00:15:34.133 --> 00:15:37.136
Mama, this girl can do magic!

00:15:37.136 --> 00:15:39.004
Really? What kind of magic?

00:15:39.004 --> 00:15:41.607
She can give you anything you wish for!

00:15:41.607 --> 00:15:44.176
What?! But you said you could
only get one wish!

00:15:44.176 --> 00:15:45.644
Uh-uh! Three wishes!

00:15:45.644 --> 00:15:46.612
That's a lie!

00:15:46.612 --> 00:15:47.746
No, it's true!

00:15:47.746 --> 00:15:49.381
Okay! Then, I want a remote-controlled...

00:15:49.381 --> 00:15:50.716
You can't have anything!

00:15:50.716 --> 00:15:51.750
And I suppose some blocks...

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:52.351
I said you can't!
And I suppose some blocks...

00:15:52.351 --> 00:15:52.751
I said you can't!

00:15:52.751 --> 00:15:55.621
Paul, Carrie gave the wish to
Mom already, didn't she?

00:15:55.621 --> 00:15:57.056
I know already.

00:15:57.056 --> 00:16:02.127
Well, I'll make one wish.
Then why don't you each make one too?

00:16:02.127 --> 00:16:03.595
Huh? What about me?

00:16:03.595 --> 00:16:07.199
Ah, the older sister, a child to the end.

00:16:07.199 --> 00:16:08.632
Oh, yeah, I suppose.

00:16:09.401 --> 00:16:11.370
Okay then, well, hmm...

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.538
I think I'II... Maybe a...

00:16:12.538 --> 00:16:14.768
What should I wish for?
And me? Let's see...

00:16:24.783 --> 00:16:27.686
That's why I'm saying no way!

00:16:27.686 --> 00:16:29.313
Come on! Don't be like that!

00:16:30.222 --> 00:16:33.025
Those are those guys from before,
aren't they, Rachel?

00:16:33.025 --> 00:16:34.460
Uh, yeah.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:38.197
They don't back off!
That's why I ran away from them!

00:16:38.197 --> 00:16:40.859
Poor Vanessa, they've got her trapped!

00:16:41.266 --> 00:16:42.534
She can take care of herself.

00:16:42.534 --> 00:16:43.660
You can say that again!

00:16:44.103 --> 00:16:45.571
You're not going to go bail her out, Amanda?

00:16:45.571 --> 00:16:47.698
Hell no, I'm staying right here.

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:50.376
Rachel, you want anything to drink?

00:16:50.376 --> 00:16:51.502
Rachel?

00:16:52.111 --> 00:16:53.635
Uh, no thanks.

00:16:53.879 --> 00:16:55.914
I'm going to step out for a little air.

00:16:55.914 --> 00:16:58.417
Okay, I'll be out later.

00:16:58.417 --> 00:17:00.285
Luke, it was your fault to begin with!

00:17:00.285 --> 00:17:01.752
Huh? What d'ya mean?

00:17:10.429 --> 00:17:11.521
Did I say something like that?

00:17:27.212 --> 00:17:29.407
What the hell? It's not like I'm some kid.

00:17:34.953 --> 00:17:36.488
Excuse me...

00:17:36.488 --> 00:17:37.823
Huh? Rachel?

00:17:37.823 --> 00:17:40.125
Teacher?

00:17:40.125 --> 00:17:41.226
It is you.

00:17:41.226 --> 00:17:43.896
I'm sorry, I'm so out of it.

00:17:43.896 --> 00:17:45.955
Oh, don't worry. I'll pick 'em up.

00:17:46.899 --> 00:17:48.700
Wow, you really have a lot of books.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:51.970
Yeah, well they say that used book
store is going out of business

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:53.335
so I went and did a little impulse shopping.

00:17:54.273 --> 00:17:55.674
Holy cow, this thing's heavy...

00:17:55.674 --> 00:17:57.209
Hit someone with it and they'll know it!

00:17:57.209 --> 00:17:58.403
I bet!

00:17:59.912 --> 00:18:01.846
I was on my way over to that coffee shop.

00:18:02.147 --> 00:18:04.016
I'll treat you to a coffee.
It's my way of saying "sorry."

00:18:04.016 --> 00:18:05.150
But I...

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:07.050
Yes, for a coffee of course.

00:18:13.826 --> 00:18:14.952
What's wrong?

00:18:15.094 --> 00:18:17.187
This is bitter, right?

00:18:18.297 --> 00:18:19.457
It's fine.

00:18:20.132 --> 00:18:21.360
It's good, try it.

00:18:26.905 --> 00:18:28.873
You have to drink slowly, and take in
the flavor while it's in your mouth.

00:18:30.109 --> 00:18:32.478
The beans here smell different than those
at the shops by your place, don't they?

00:18:32.478 --> 00:18:34.469
I have no idea!

00:18:35.814 --> 00:18:37.714
You can add cream if you want.

00:18:38.217 --> 00:18:38.884
No, it's fine.

00:18:38.884 --> 00:18:39.351
Huh? It's fine?
No, it's fine.

00:18:39.351 --> 00:18:40.283
Huh? It's fine?

00:18:40.486 --> 00:18:41.475
Yeah.

00:18:41.887 --> 00:18:46.415
You'll learn to appreciate it once
you've grown up a bit.

00:18:46.992 --> 00:18:48.721
Oh, you think you're so cool.

00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:53.232
Well, I'm sure you've thawed
yourself out by now.

00:18:53.232 --> 00:18:55.564
If you're ever feeling down,
give this book a read.

00:18:56.101 --> 00:18:58.036
In order to grow up?

00:18:58.036 --> 00:19:00.061
Naw, because it'll put you to sleep.

00:19:05.744 --> 00:19:06.938
Huh?!

00:19:11.116 --> 00:19:13.252
What's wrong? You're not going to eat it?

00:19:13.252 --> 00:19:14.219
Well...

00:19:15.254 --> 00:19:16.448
No...

00:19:19.124 --> 00:19:21.490
So the rent, does it look like you can pay it?

00:19:22.461 --> 00:19:23.729
It's paid.

00:19:23.729 --> 00:19:24.753
Huh?

00:19:24.997 --> 00:19:26.988
So, you did go borrow some
money from your brother.

00:19:27.799 --> 00:19:28.534
Yeah.

00:19:28.534 --> 00:19:29.535
Really...
Yeah.

00:19:29.535 --> 00:19:32.470
Well, things happen as long
as you're alive, you know.

00:19:33.205 --> 00:19:34.473
As long as you're alive...

00:19:34.473 --> 00:19:36.475
Well, I guess I'm just quoting my grandpa,

00:19:36.475 --> 00:19:37.840
trying to sound all wise and cool.

00:19:39.077 --> 00:19:43.549
Yeah, stuff like this happens
because I'm alive, huh?

00:19:43.549 --> 00:19:44.917
Yeah, exactly!

00:19:44.917 --> 00:19:49.354
You just find a job as quickly as you can,
then pay him back!

00:19:49.354 --> 00:19:50.616
Yeah...

00:19:50.856 --> 00:19:53.017
And I can help you look for one.

00:19:54.993 --> 00:19:56.119
Yeah...

00:20:00.632 --> 00:20:04.500
Doctor, you still haven't started giving
her the other medication.

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:09.464
Um, you can't just...

00:20:30.295 --> 00:20:31.728
Who's there?

00:20:33.699 --> 00:20:36.668
You... What's your name?

00:20:40.072 --> 00:20:41.403
Your name?

00:20:42.674 --> 00:20:43.868
Herve.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:48.305
Herve... That's a nice name.

00:20:49.982 --> 00:20:52.610
Are these people here your family?

00:20:54.019 --> 00:20:55.281
Yes...

00:20:56.221 --> 00:20:58.587
Hey, Herve...

00:20:59.758 --> 00:21:03.250
Do you know my name?

00:21:05.297 --> 00:21:08.289
My name...

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:30.522
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:21:30.522 --> 00:21:32.820
One, two, everybody go!

00:21:40.932 --> 00:21:43.201
The time has come! It's now! But still!

00:21:43.201 --> 00:21:45.804
It always starts with the tears in your eyes

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:47.906
If every weighed-out day

00:21:47.906 --> 00:21:50.108
You leave feeling sick, fly high

00:21:50.108 --> 00:21:51.677
Yesterday's failures? They don't mean a thing!

00:21:51.677 --> 00:21:53.812
Tomorrow's worries? They don't mean a thing!

00:21:53.812 --> 00:21:55.947
What's always important is this moment

00:21:55.947 --> 00:21:58.541
So it goes up to the top, top, top, top

00:22:07.059 --> 00:22:08.794
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:22:08.794 --> 00:22:10.195
Gather around, my comrades

00:22:10.195 --> 00:22:11.330
If the dream you haven't had doesn't fade away

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:13.098
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:22:13.098 --> 00:22:14.966
So don't care, babe!

00:22:14.966 --> 00:22:18.603
I'm not going to ask you the reason

00:22:18.603 --> 00:22:22.841
We'll protect you

00:22:22.841 --> 00:22:25.477
So it's okay even if they don't like you

00:22:25.477 --> 00:22:29.981
Even if they laugh at you

00:22:29.981 --> 00:22:33.018
Just keep going down that road you believe in

00:22:33.018 --> 00:22:35.620
Your tears are

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:39.825
Two of this world's treasures beyond compare

00:22:39.825 --> 00:22:42.661
I will simply keep on singing

00:22:42.661 --> 00:22:49.801
So I won't lose it and it will reach you

00:22:49.801 --> 00:22:52.037
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:22:52.037 --> 00:22:54.139
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:22:54.139 --> 00:22:56.369
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:23:00.645 --> 00:23:04.604
Some cling to dim hope;
some are cast to the wayside.

00:23:04.983 --> 00:23:07.052
And yet others tremble with rage.

00:23:07.052 --> 00:23:09.955
They too had families they wanted to protect,

00:23:09.955 --> 00:23:09.988
Episode #10
Bewilderment
They too had families they wanted to protect,

00:23:09.988 --> 00:23:12.157
Episode #10
Bewilderment
and their own happy lives.

